# Japanese translations for scitex-hub.
#
# SCOPE: public/legal surfaces only — the landing page and the commerce/legal
# pages. The signed-in app interior stays English for now, per the operator
# (2026-08-23): 「日本語、英語、意外は私が見てもわからないので今のところは非対応で
# 問題ないです」 — Japanese and English only.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS: the landing page is read by investors and lenders in Japan.
# Operator, 2026-08-23: 「日本の会社でビジコンやら融資やらでも外部の方が見られた方が
# 良いので。日本の方で英語が使いにくいと思う方はたくさんいらっしゃいます」
#
# REVIEW STATUS: these strings were drafted by scitex-hub and are NOT yet
# approved by the operator. They are investor-facing copy about his company;
# read them on the running site rather than trusting this file.
#
# WHERE THE GETTEXT TOOLS ACTUALLY EXIST. Measured 2026-08-23, because an
# earlier revision of this header told the reader to run `makemessages` in a
# place where it cannot run:
#
#     agent container        xgettext ABSENT   msgfmt ABSENT
#     bare host (compute-03) xgettext ABSENT   msgfmt ABSENT
#     dev django container   xgettext PRESENT  msgfmt PRESENT
#     prod image             (msgfmt ABSENT; babel present)
#
# REGENERATE — only inside the dev container, which is the one place with
# xgettext. `makemessages` shells out to it exactly as `compilemessages` shells
# out to msgfmt, so it fails identically everywhere else:
#
#     docker exec scitex-hub-dev-django-1 python manage.py makemessages -l ja
#
# COMPILE — anywhere, including prod. Use the babel-based step, NOT
# `django-admin compilemessages`: msgfmt is absent from the PRODUCTION image, so
# compilemessages would succeed in dev and fail where users are.
#
#     python scripts/i18n/compile_catalogs.py
#
# This runs automatically from both entrypoints on every container start.
msgid ""
msgstr ""
"Project-Id-Version: scitex-hub\n"
"Report-Msgid-Bugs-To: \n"
"POT-Creation-Date: 2026-08-23 07:45+0000\n"
"PO-Revision-Date: 2026-08-23 07:45+0000\n"
"Last-Translator: scitex-hub <info@scitex.ai>\n"
"Language-Team: Japanese\n"
"Language: ja\n"
"MIME-Version: 1.0\n"
"Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8\n"
"Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit\n"
"Plural-Forms: nplurals=1; plural=0;\n"

